<report>
<line><title>Fully nested/hierarchical random analysis of variance</title></line>
<line></line>
<line>Variables:<in>tlist</in></line>
<line></line>
<table>
<tr><th>Source of Variation</th><th>Sum Squares</th><th>DF</th><th>Mean Square</th></tr>
<tr><td>Between Groups</td><td><in>grp_sum</in></td><td><in>grp_df</in></td><td><in>grp_mean</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Between Subgroups within Groups</td><td><in>sub_sum</in></td><td><in>sub_df</in></td><td><in>sub_mean</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Residual</td><td><in>res_sum</in></td><td><in>res_df</in></td><td><in>res_mean</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Total</td><td><in>tot_sum</in></td><td><in>tot_df</in></td></tr>
</table>
<line></line>
<line>F (VR between groups) = <in>f_1</in>  <in>p_1</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>F (using group/subgroup msqr) = <in>f_2</in>  <in>p_2</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>F (VR between subgroups within groups) = <in>f_3</in>  <in>p_3</in></line>
</report>
